WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
As we kick off Beauty Week, I can't have thought

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.990
or dreamt to have done it with anyone like you.

3
00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.440
When do you feel most beautiful?

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.360
I have to say, I feel pretty beautiful talking

5
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.130
to you because it's amazing to talk

6
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.570
to another woman you admire and bounce back and forth

7
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.217
with her and look at her beautiful, bouncy hair.

8
00:00:20.217 --> 00:00:22.110
You have really bouncy hair.
(audience softly laughing)

9
00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.723
Thank you, it's all Mr. Daniel.

10
00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:27.361
Thank you, Mr. Daniel, for blessing us.

11
00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:29.870
(audience loudly laughing)

12
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.160
And I feel beautiful when I'm directing.

13
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.760
I love to feel like I'm in charge

14
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.902
but I love to do it in a way that's gentle

15
00:00:37.902 --> 00:00:41.130
and in a way that honors other people's creative process,

16
00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.560
and just to gently move a process along

17
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.460
and to express my vision and bounce off someone else's.

18
00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.390
And I love to just wear those headphones

19
00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.700
and wear those boots and tromp around

20
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.670 line:15%
and like midday, on a long shoot day

21
00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.130 line:15%
and like, you've just had your third coffee of the day

22
00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.820 line:15%
and you're about to like charge up a hill,

23
00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.140
like that's a really good feeling.

24
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.300
I relate to you because I feel like I grew up,

25
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.460
I was like an adult, I wasn't a kid.

26
00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.310
I never felt like a kid.

27
00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.000
I was always interested in

28
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.660
a bigger-picture thinking, living in conversations

29
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.380
even when I was young.

30
00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.950
You know, I didn't live my childhood

31
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.710
in the public eye the way that you did,

32
00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:25.600
but I've lived a very pivotal period from 23 to 34

33
00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.200
under a specific kind of scrutiny.

34
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.620
And I think watching the way

35
00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.240
that you have navigated that so gracefully

36
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.130
and that you have actually carved your own path

37
00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.270
and actually decided to define your own chapters,

38
00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.580
that's something that I've taken a lot of heart in

39
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.660
at moments where I felt like other people were

40
00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:47.110
maybe making those definitions for me.

41
00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.750
So your journey has not gone unnoticed

42
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.130
by this little wanderer.

43
00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:55.210
Thank you so much for that.

44
00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.800
One of the things I love about you

45
00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.200
and that I've tried to do a lot

46
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.210
in my life is be open to listening to all of it

47
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.870
and putting it through your own funnel,

48
00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.170
however you interpret it.

49
00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:13.080
A lot of people, it's hard to hear everything.

50
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.630
It's not easy, takes a spine and a sense of humor.

51
00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.800
Yeah, and there've been times

52
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.040
that people have told me things,

53
00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.970 line:15%
by people, I mean the public,

54
00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.290 line:15%
that have been really important for me to hear,

55
00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.930 line:15%
things that were really important for me to hear.

56
00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.230
And there've been times that I've received criticism

57
00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:37.230
that I knew was the voice of a system, a patriarchal system.

58
00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.300
A system that didn't like to hear noisy women.

59
00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.730
A system that didn't like to hear women

60
00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.050
who wanted to talk about their bodies,

61
00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.350
women who want to talk about sex,

62
00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.770
women who want to talk about their libidos,

63
00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:50.280
women who want to talk about their anger.

64
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.780
And I really had to try to separate what was useful

65
00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.500
and valid criticism that I needed to internalize

66
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.330
in order to grow and become the person

67
00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.700
that I knew I wanted to be.

68
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.380
And yes, it does take being able to really hear

69
00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.053
and also really be able to laugh at yourself.

70
00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.420
Lena's journey to self-love has included

71
00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.670
some serious health struggles.

72
00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.100
She lives with Ehlers-Danlos syndrome,

73
00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.270
which causes joint pain and other issues,

74
00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.350
as well as endometriosis

75
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:26.193
for which she underwent a hysterectomy at age 31.

76
00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.070
Now you've talked a lot about health.

77
00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.740
You mentioned the body and just everything

78
00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.410
that a lot of people are not comfortable talking about,

79
00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.800
they're not comfortable listening to.

80
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:44.670
This is men and women, this is a genderless issue.

81
00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.950
Will you talk to me about your health,

82
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.350
where you've been, where it's at now?

83
00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:53.800
Because I have been wrapped in your journey as a woman.

84
00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.250
Well, that means so much.

85
00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:59.050
And from the beginning of my health struggle,

86
00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.100
something that I was really committed to was the idea

87
00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.890 line:15%
that I was not going to keep it a secret

88
00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:07.440 line:15%
because we're in a culture that sees illness as weakness.

89
00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.150 line:15%
We're in a culture that sees sick women

90
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.500
as hysterical women, and we're in a business, you and I,

91
00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.350
that doesn't look kindly on illness

92
00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:18.180
because we, people are working at such a pace

93
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.060
with so much money involved

94
00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:23.516
that for someone to be in any way

95
00:04:23.516 --> 00:04:27.990
unable to show up or potentially a liability.

96
00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.723
And so I wanted to bring it out into the open.

97
00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.310
I knew for a long time that I was sick with endometriosis.

98
00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:38.163 line:15%
It caused enormous amount of pain, health challenges,

99
00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.360 line:15%
but I also knew something deeper was going on with my body.

100
00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.210 line:15%
And so I undertook an exploration

101
00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.320
and came to understand that I also have

102
00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.440
an underlying health condition called Ehlers-Danlos syndrome

103
00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:54.280
which is a connective tissue disease that causes

104
00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.290
like diffuse musculoskeletal pain and a number

105
00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.480
of other sort of random but interlinked symptoms.

106
00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.670
I also have a form of autoimmune arthritis

107
00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.330
that is associated with it,

108
00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:08.880 line:15%
and so I also deal with autoimmune issues at the same time.

109
00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:12.320 line:15%
And so all of that came together in my 20s

110
00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.590 line:15%
to make a pretty miserable,

111
00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:14.580
when I wasn't treating it,

112
00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.090
to make a pretty miserable health picture

113
00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:20.650
and sort of culminated in my having a hysterectomy

114
00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.480
and one of my ovaries removed at 31.

115
00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.543
Which was terrifying,

116
00:05:25.543 --> 00:05:27.740
not just because it was a massive surgery,

117
00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.210
but because I really want to be a mom

118
00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.120
and had always thought that I was going

119
00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.700
to do it in the traditional way.

120
00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.090
And I don't think I realized how much I was going

121
00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:41.820
to grieve that and how intense that process was going to be.

122
00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.100
And I have to say though, the process of being able

123
00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.330
to be open about that and write about that

124
00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:51.650
and understand how many other women, how many other people,

125
00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.060
how many other couples have grieved that alone

126
00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:58.210
and together was one of the most healing things

127
00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.758
I've ever experienced.

128
00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:02.341
(bright music)

